<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince Vijaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">traditionally 543–505 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Vijaya is the legendary first king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, said in the Pali chronicles to have been exiled from northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and to have landed on the island with 700 followers on the day of the Buddha's death, traditionally 543 BCE. He married the Yakkha woman Kuveni, founded the settlement of Tambapanni and later took a bride from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> country. The Sinhalese traditionally trace their origins to him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-vijaya.jpg" alt="Prince Vijaya" width="320" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo Dharma from Sadao, Thailand · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Consecration_Of_King_Sinhala-Prince_Vijaya_(Detail_From_The_Ajanta_Mural_Of_Cave_No_17).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
